Regeneration: re-copy from the pinned zed reference tree. The vendored zed
snapshot is the one at commit 70351f5's date (2026-09) in this repository.

Local patches (the crates.io grammar releases lag zed's forks):
- cpp.scm: dropped C++20 module patterns and the "export"/"import"/"module"
  keyword tokens (absent from tree-sitter-cpp 0.23.4).
- javascript.scm: dropped zed-fork TypeScript-flavored patterns
  (type_arguments, nested_type_identifier, required/optional_parameter,
  type_identifier, …) and TS-only keyword tokens.

Not vendored:
- markdown: zed's highlights.scm targets zed's markdown grammar fork and is
  incompatible with tree-sitter-markdown 0.7.1 (no `pipe_table`, different
  heading structure). Revisit with a markdown grammar upgrade.
- html: zed ships no html grammar; the endpoint uses the tree-sitter-html
  crate's own bundled HIGHLIGHTS_QUERY directly (no file here).

html.scm is NOT from zed (zed ships no html grammar); it is the
tree-sitter-html crate's own bundled HIGHLIGHTS_QUERY (MIT, tree-sitter
grammars upstream), written out here so every language loads through the
same include_str! path.
